<BaseLayout
  title="Sell Your Texas Land"
  description="Selling a farm, ranch, or recreational property in Texas? Honest pricing, professional presentation, and marketing that reaches real land buyers."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Sell your land for what it's honestly worth</h1>
      <p>
        Land that's priced on hope sits. Land that's priced on evidence —
        comparable sales, productive capacity, water, and what buyers in this
        market are actually paying — sells. Honest Acres Group starts every
        listing with a straight conversation about both.
      </p>

      <h2>What sellers get</h2>
      <div class="cards">
        <div class="card"><h3>Honest pricing guidance</h3><p>A valuation grounded in the local market and the land itself — carrying capacity, water, improvements, and habitat — not a number picked to win a listing.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Presentation that respects the place</h3><p>Professional photos, maps, and a property story that tells buyers what the land does, season to season.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Reach beyond the sign</h3><p>Exposure on the major land platforms, our website and blog, social channels, YouTube, and a growing list of qualified Texas land buyers.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>A fiduciary in your corner</h3><p>Straight answers at every offer and negotiation, from a broker-represented team that works this country itself.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h2>Thinking about it?</h2>
      <p>
        Even if you're a year out, an honest valuation today helps you plan —
        which fences, water, or habitat work would actually pay back, and
        which wouldn't. That conversation costs nothing.
      </p>
      <p><a class="btn btn-green" href="/contact/">Ask for an honest valuation</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
